Build a pomodoro timer app in a single HTML file.

**Core timer**: Display a large circular countdown in the center showing MM:SS format. Track work/break/long-break phases cycling continuously. Work session is 25 min (default), short break is 5 min (default), long break is 15 min (default). After every 4 pomodoros (configurable), the next break is a long break instead. Display current phase (Work/Break/Long break), pomodoro number (#1, #2, etc), and total time remaining.

**Controls**: Start/Pause button that auto-starts the next session when one ends (no manual transition needed). Skip button advances to next phase immediately. Reset button returns to the beginning. Space key toggles start/pause.

**Circular ring progress**: SVG circle that drains as time counts down, using different accent colors for work (pink) vs break (green). Ring color and overall theme follow the selected theme.

**Settings panel** (gear icon, top-left, toggles open/closed): Editable inputs for work duration, break duration, long break duration, and pomodoros-per-long-break (all validated 1–120 min). New setting: checkbox toggle "Tick last 10 sec" (default off) that plays a soft, brief tick sound each second during the final 10 seconds of any session. Persist all settings to localStorage.

**Theme picker** (top-right, color dot + "Theme" button): Six themes—Tokyo Night (default, pink/green), Ocean (cyan), Forest (amber/green), Rose (pink/purple), Ember (orange/yellow), Light (warm light bg)—each with distinct color palette. Persist theme choice to localStorage. 

**Audio**: Generate a gentle bell chime (three rising notes for work-done, two-note callback for break-done) using Web Audio API. When tick toggle is on, play a subtle high-frequency tick during the last 10 seconds. All audio is synthesized; no audio files needed.

**Daily counter**: Show "🍅 N pomodoros completed today" below the controls. Persist per-day using localStorage with date key; auto-reset at midnight. Dynamically pluralize the label.

**Accuracy**: Use timestamp-based timing (Date.now()) to keep the timer accurate even if the browser tab is throttled. Render updates ~4 times per second.

**UX**: Settings/theme panels close when clicking outside or pressing Escape. Pressing Escape closes both menus. Display a hint below the daily counter. Make the UI responsive and centered; use monospace numbers for timer display.
